{"content":[{"c":["ADRAMMELECH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Son of the Assyrian monarch Sennacherib. This Adrammelech and his brother Sharezer killed their father in the temple of Nisroch in Nineveh (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.37","r":"2Kgs.19.37","rawR":"2Kgs.19.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.37","value":"2Kgs.19.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 19:37"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.38","r":"Isa.37.38","rawR":"Isa.37.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.38","value":"Isa.37.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 37:38"},"). The nonbiblical ",{"c":["Babylonian Chronicles"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," also refers to this assassination but does not name the sons."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Sennacherib_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Sennacherib_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Sennacherib_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sennacherib"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Deity worshiped by the Syrians from Sepharvaim whom the Assyrians resettled in Samaria. Adrammelech was a god to whom children were sacrificed by the Sepharvites (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","r":"2Kgs.17.31","rawR":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.31","value":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 17:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Mesopotamia_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Mesopotamia"},"; ",{"href":"?item=SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SyriaSyrians_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Syria, Syrians"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Adrammelech","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 19:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.37","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.37","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.37"},{"anchorText":"Is 37:38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.38","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.38","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.38"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 17:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.31","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.31","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6cfbc81a6b2c3ce47d9e3f67a7d7fe5bc3d9755e125c83a51e3525d07150d7de","sourceItemName":"Adrammelech","sourceItemOrder":138,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Adrammelech","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Adrammelech","title":"Adrammelech","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}